3.2.37 ‘control-polygon-interface’
----------------------------------

A grob used to visualize the control polygon of a Bézier curve (such as
a tie or a slur), for ease of tweaking.

User-settable properties:
.........................

     ‘extroversion’ (number)
          For polygons, how the thickness of the line is spread on each
          side of the exact polygon with ideal zero thickness.  If this
          is 0, the middle of line is on the polygon.  If 1, the line
          sticks out of the polygon.  If -1, the outer side of the line
          is exactly on the polygon.  Other numeric values are
          interpolated.

     ‘filled’ (boolean)
          Whether an object is filled with ink.

Internal properties:
....................

     ‘bezier’ (graphical (layout) object)
          A pointer to a Bézier curve, for use by control points and
          polygons.

   This grob interface is used in the following graphical object(s):
*note ControlPolygon::.


